DataFlyerSCSI @VER@
===================

A driver for the Expansion Systems DataFlyer 1200 SCSI+ on AmigaOS 3.1 and
newer: dataflyer.device, with RDBMount to mount the SCSI drives at boot and
tools to test and look at drives. The original SCSIPlus, DFMount and
ExpXDS.device are not needed any more.

Install: double-click Install_DataFlyerSCSI. It copies the driver to DEVS:
and RDBMount to C:, puts the tools where you say, mounts the drives it finds,
adds the boot line to S:User-Startup and turns the original software's lines
into comments. Run it again to update or to remove.

The manual is DataFlyerSCSI.guide (double-click it); it explains the card, the
driver, every tool, HDToolBox, and what to do when something does not work.

What is where:
  Devs/dataflyer.device        the driver
  C/RDBMount                   mounts the partitions of SCSI drives (boot)
  Tools/                       flytest, flystat, flyprobe, flyirq, flychange, devlist,
                               fcmp, flyread, tick, UserStartup.rexx
  Storage/DOSDrivers/CD0       a mount file for a SCSI CD-ROM (CDFileSystem)
  DataFlyerSCSI.guide          the manual
  LICENSE                      GNU GPL version 3

Source and bug reports: https://github.com/lainejones/DataFlyerSCSI
